# Goodix fingerprint reader — disable USB autosuspend
#
# WHY: usb 3-6 (27c6:659a "Goodix USB2.0 MISC", driven from userspace by
# libfprint's goodixmoc) sits in a continuous reset loop on this machine because
# it fails to resume from USB autosuspend. Measured reset counts per boot:
#
#   boot -1 (abrupt): 851      boot -3 (clean, 2.7 days): 12
#   boot -4 (abrupt): 469      boot -8 (clean, ~22h):      4
#   boot  0 (current): 734 in ~13h
#
# Every reset targets 3-6 and nothing else. Default state was power/control=auto
# with autosuspend_delay_ms=2000 (global usbcore.autosuspend=2) and no udev rule
# matching 27c6 anywhere on the system.
#
# 851 spurious device resets per boot is a defect worth fixing on its own merits.
# It is also a candidate contributor to the freezes: a USB device that fails to
# resume can block the system PM resume path, and boot -1's final kernel line was
# one of these resets, logged the instant the lock screen opened the device.
#
# ORDERING: must sort AFTER /usr/lib/udev/rules.d/60-autosuspend.rules, which sets
# power/control="auto" for USB devices. A 50- prefix loses that race (verified with
# `udevadm test /sys/bus/usb/devices/3-6`), hence 99-.
#
# See syshardening/PLAN.md Phase 1a-bis.

ACTION=="add", SUBSYSTEM=="usb", ATTR{idVendor}=="27c6", ATTR{idProduct}=="659a", TEST=="power/control", ATTR{power/control}="on"
